   },
   "skos:definition": "The Synoptic scene in the Jerusalem Temple (Mark 12:18-27; Matthew 22:23-33; Luke 20:27-40) in which Sadducees, who denied the resurrection, pose a riddle about a widow married to seven brothers, and Jesus answers that the risen do not marry and that God's words to Moses at the burning bush show he is \"the God of the living.\"",
