   "skos:broader": {
    "@id": "bg:the-bible"
   },
   "skos:definition": "The single, unfolding story that Christians read across the Bible's many books: God creates a good world, humanity turns away, God calls Abraham and Israel, comes in Jesus the Messiah, sends the church to all nations, and promises a renewed creation.",
