   },
   "skos:definition": "The sanctuary of Israel's God on the Temple Mount in Jerusalem: first built by Solomon and burned by the Babylonians, rebuilt after the exile and lavishly expanded by Herod, then destroyed by Rome in AD 70; in Scripture the place where God set his name among his people, a theme the New Testament carries over to Jesus himself and to the church.",
