  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-interprets-scripture/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:scripture-interprets-scripture"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Matthew 4:1-11, where do Jesus's replies in verses 4 and 7 come from, and what situation of Israel's were those words first spoken into?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-interprets-scripture/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:scripture-interprets-scripture"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What does the devil leave out when he uses Psalm 91 in Matthew 4:6, and what difference does Deuteronomy 6:16 make?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-interprets-scripture/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:scripture-interprets-scripture"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to Luke 24:27 and 24:44-45, how did the risen Jesus help his disciples understand the Scriptures as a whole?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-interprets-scripture/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:scripture-interprets-scripture"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What did the people of Beroea do with Paul's preaching in Acts 17:11, and what would it look like for your study group to do the same?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-interprets-scripture/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:scripture-interprets-scripture"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Is there a verse you have built a lot on by itself? Which other passages on the same subject could you read alongside it this week?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-interprets-scripture/example",
   "@type": "bgo:Rewrite",
   "bgo:after": "Psalm 91 is a song of trust for the one who makes God their refuge; Jesus, offered this very verse as a dare, answered from Deuteronomy 6:16 that we must not put God to the test.",
   "bgo:before": "God promised his angels will catch me, so I can push my luck and he has to rescue me.",
   "bgo:situation": "Someone reads Psalm 91:11-12, \"they will bear you up in their hands\", and concludes that God guarantees protection from the consequences of any deliberate risk they choose to take.",
   "bgo:why": "In Matthew 4:5-7 the devil quotes the psalm on its own, and Jesus answers \"Again, it is written\", letting another Scripture show how the promise is meant to be held."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-interprets-scripture/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Scripture Interprets Scripture",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-interprets-scripture/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-interprets-scripture/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-interprets-scripture/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-interprets-scripture/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-interprets-scripture/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-interprets-scripture/howto/6"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-interprets-scripture/howto/7"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-interprets-scripture/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Read the passage in its own setting first (paragraph, chapter, book) so you know what it says before you compare it with anything else."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-interprets-scripture/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Look up the cross-references in a study Bible, starting with any passage the text quotes or echoes, and read each one in its own context too."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-interprets-scripture/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "When the New Testament quotes the Old, open the Old Testament passage and ask what it meant there and why the New Testament writer reached for it."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-interprets-scripture/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Gather the passages that treat the same subject directly and at length, and let these clearer, fuller passages shed light on brief or puzzling ones."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-interprets-scripture/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Check that each link is a real link of meaning, not just a shared English word that may mean different things in different books."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-interprets-scripture/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "When passages seem to pull in different directions, hold both and ask how they fit together before choosing one and setting the other aside."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/scripture-interprets-scripture/howto/7",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 7,
   "schema:text": "Test your conclusion against the main lines of the whole biblical story and, as your church teaches, against its wider reading of the faith."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/second-temple-judaism/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:second-temple-judaism"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to Nehemiah 8:1-8, what did Ezra and the Levites do with the Law of Moses, and how did the people respond?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/second-temple-judaism/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:second-temple-judaism"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Luke 4:16-21, what does Jesus do \"as was his custom\" on the Sabbath, and what does that tell us about his own Jewish practice?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/second-temple-judaism/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:second-temple-judaism"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Acts 23:6-8 shows Pharisees and Sadducees disagreeing about the resurrection. What does that suggest about how varied Jewish belief was in Paul's day?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/second-temple-judaism/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:second-temple-judaism"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Which familiar Gospel scenes (a synagogue reading, a Temple feast, a debate with Pharisees) do you now picture differently, and why might knowing Jesus's Jewish world deepen your reading of him?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/septuagint/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:septuagint"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Compare Psalm 40:6 in an English Bible with Hebrews 10:5. What does each say God prepared, and why might they differ?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/septuagint/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:septuagint"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Acts 15:17, how does James's quotation of Amos 9:12 support welcoming Gentiles, and how does the Hebrew wording of Amos read?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/septuagint/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:septuagint"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Why do you think the apostles were content to quote Scripture in a translation their hearers could understand?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/septuagint/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:septuagint"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "How might knowing about the Septuagint help you talk graciously with a Christian whose Old Testament has more books than yours?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/sermon-on-the-mount/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:sermon-on-the-mount"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Who is listening when Jesus begins to teach in Matthew 5:1-2, and who is listening when he finishes in Matthew 7:28-29? Why might both groups matter?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/sermon-on-the-mount/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:sermon-on-the-mount"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Matthew 5:17-20, what does Jesus say he came to do with the Law and the Prophets?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/sermon-on-the-mount/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:sermon-on-the-mount"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Read the three examples of \"secret\" devotion in Matthew 6:1-18 (giving, prayer, fasting). What do they have in common, and which one most challenges your own habits?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/sermon-on-the-mount/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:sermon-on-the-mount"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "The sermon ends with two builders (Matthew 7:24-27). What is the difference between them, and what would \"doing\" one of these teachings look like for you or your group this week?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/song-of-the-sea/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:song-of-the-sea"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Exodus 14:31 says the people \"feared Yahweh\" and believed. How does the song that follows in Exodus 15:1 turn that fear and faith into worship?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/song-of-the-sea/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:song-of-the-sea"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "List the names and pictures the song uses for God in Exodus 15:2-3 and 15:11. Which one surprises you, and why?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/song-of-the-sea/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:song-of-the-sea"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Verses 1-12 look back at the sea; verses 13-17 look ahead. Where is God leading his people, according to verses 13 and 17?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/song-of-the-sea/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:song-of-the-sea"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What does Exodus 15:18 add to the whole song? How does it prepare you to hear Jesus announce the kingdom of God?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/song-of-the-sea/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:song-of-the-sea"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Who is Miriam (Exodus 15:20), and what does it mean that the women answer the song with drums and dancing?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/song-of-the-sea/check/6",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:song-of-the-sea"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Revelation 15:3 the redeemed sing \"the song of Moses ... and the song of the Lamb\". What rescue in your own life or your church's story would you put into words of praise?"
  },
