  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/suffering-and-lament/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:suffering-and-lament"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Psalm 13 asks \"How long?\" four times in two verses. What changes in verses 5-6, and has the psalmist's situation changed by then?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/suffering-and-lament/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:suffering-and-lament"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Psalm 88 ends in darkness, without a turn to praise. Why might God have included a prayer like this in Scripture?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/suffering-and-lament/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:suffering-and-lament"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Job 42:7-8, God says the friends did not speak rightly about him \"as my servant Job has.\" What had the friends said, and what had Job done?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/suffering-and-lament/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:suffering-and-lament"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Jesus prays the opening words of Psalm 22 from the cross (Matthew 27:46). How does knowing the whole psalm shape the way you hear his cry?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/suffering-and-lament/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:suffering-and-lament"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What do I find hardest to say honestly to God? What would it look like to pray a lament psalm in my own words this week?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-exodus/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:the-exodus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Exodus 3:7-8, what four things does God say he has seen, heard, known and come down to do for his people?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-exodus/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:the-exodus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to Exodus 12:26-27, what are parents to tell their children when they ask about the Passover, and why might Israel have built a question into the ritual?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-exodus/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:the-exodus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "How does Exodus 20:2 connect the commandments to the rescue from Egypt? What difference does it make that God saves first and then gives the law?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-exodus/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:the-exodus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Paul calls Christ \"our Passover\" (1 Corinthians 5:7) and says the wilderness events \"happened to them by way of example\" (1 Corinthians 10:11). Where do you see your own story in Israel's — both the rescue and the grumbling afterwards?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-story-of-the-bible/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:the-story-of-the-bible"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Genesis 12:1-3, what does God promise Abram, and who will finally be blessed through him?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-story-of-the-bible/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:the-story-of-the-bible"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to Luke 24:27 and Luke 24:44, which parts of the Scriptures did the risen Jesus say were about him?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-story-of-the-bible/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:the-story-of-the-bible"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Compare Genesis 3:23-24 with Revelation 22:1-3. What was lost at the beginning of the story, and what is restored at the end?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-story-of-the-bible/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:the-story-of-the-bible"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Why might it matter whether the Old Testament closes with Cyrus's call to \"go up\" (2 Chronicles 36:23) or with the promise of Elijah (Malachi 4:5)?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-story-of-the-bible/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:the-story-of-the-bible"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "If the church lives in the \"act\" between Pentecost and the new creation, what would faithful \"improvising\" look like in your own congregation this year?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-temple/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:the-temple"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to 2 Samuel 7, David wanted to build God a house. What \"house\" does God promise to build for David instead, and who will build the Temple?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-temple/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:the-temple"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In 1 Kings 8:27-30, Solomon says heaven itself cannot contain God. If that is so, what was the Temple for, according to his prayer?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-temple/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:the-temple"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In John 2:18-22, what did Jesus mean by \"this temple\", and when did his disciples finally understand it?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-temple/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:the-temple"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Paul tells the Corinthian church, \"ye are the temple of God\" (1 Corinthians 3:16, KJV). How might seeing your congregation, and not only a building, as God's dwelling change the way you treat one another?"
  }
 ]
